 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Quote Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a quote form?\", \"a\": \"A quote form is the page a customer fills in to ask what a job will cost. It collects the details that set the price, such as size, quantity, location and timing. The business replies with a firm figure.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to make a quote form?\", \"a\": \"Start with your rates and the questions that change them, then pick the jobs simple enough to price on screen. Describe both to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> and it builds the form with your pricing applied. Each request is saved as a row you can filter.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a quote form template include?\", \"a\": \"A quote form template should include every question that changes your price, such as floor area, plus an upload field when photos help. The quote you send back is a separate document that carries a quote number and expiry date above the priced line items and tax.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can quote forms calculate a price automatically?\", \"a\": \"Yes, for jobs your rates fully describe. A form can apply a base price and add a fixed amount for each extra, such as $40 per additional room, while the customer answers. Emergent writes that pricing logic from rates you describe in plain English. Anything outside your rules should go to an estimator for a firm number.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a job estimate form the same as a quote form?\", \"a\": \"No. A job estimate form produces an approximate figure that can change once work starts. A quote is a firm price for a defined scope, which the client accepts or declines. Use the estimate while the scope is still unclear, and the quote once it is fixed.\"},{\"q\": \"Where can I get a free quote form?\", \"a\": \"Form builders and template sites publish free quote form designs. Emergent is free to start, and its free tier covers building and publishing a form. Any free version still needs your own rates and questions before it can price a job.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is an online quote form better than a paper one?\", \"a\": \"For most service businesses, yes. A PDF quote form gets printed and filled in by hand, then someone retypes the answers before the job can be priced. An online form checks each answer as it arrives and keeps every request in one table. Emergent forms carry no response caps, even in your busiest month.\"},{\"q\": \"How is a quote request form different from placing an order?\", \"a\": \"A quote request form asks what something will cost before the customer commits. An <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/order-form'>order form</a> takes a purchase at a known price, often with payment. Custom work usually starts with the first, and fixed-price items with the second.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes on a job estimate form?\", \"a\": \"A job estimate form records the site address, the work requested, measurements, and photos. Add the visit date and the name of whoever took the measurements. An estimator pricing the job a week later then knows where each number came from.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes a simple quote form work?\", \"a\": \"Keep it short and tie every question to the price, with contact details last. The best quote forms ask fewer questions than you expect. When a visitor only wants a call back, a lead capture form fits better.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}